{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41737282",
      "title": "Don't Store Files Locally On The Filesystem!",
      "sourceHash": "1d92f39a7c4014b5117beb39e38ac5d2309609ebb9c56f7ad5b252be07d3516f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 3.57,
          "en": "So now that we understood how caching worked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.57,
          "end": 6.6,
          "en": "and we fixed that problem related to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.6,
          "end": 9.03,
          "en": "let's focus on that missing image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.03,
          "end": 11.4,
          "en": "Why was that image missing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.4,
          "end": 13.23,
          "en": "when we added a new meal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.23,
          "end": 15.633,
          "en": "whilst running this production server?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.95,
          "end": 18.72,
          "en": "Well, the image was missing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.72,
          "end": 21.93,
          "en": "because we store those images in this public folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.93,
          "end": 24.3,
          "en": "and they're in the images folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.3,
          "end": 28.38,
          "en": "The problem with this approach just is that this folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.38,
          "end": 31.35,
          "en": "is available during development,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.35,
          "end": 32.85,
          "en": "but for production,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.85,
          "end": 37.85,
          "en": "it's actually copied into this .next folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.86,
          "end": 40.41,
          "en": "and it's this .next folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.41,
          "end": 43.71,
          "en": "which also contains all those cached pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.71,
          "end": 46.41,
          "en": "and so on, hat will be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.41,
          "end": 50.49,
          "en": "by the running NextJS production server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.49,
          "end": 53.67,
          "en": "If you then thereafter add new images",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.67,
          "end": 56.88,
          "en": "into the public folder, those will be ignored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.88,
          "end": 59.73,
          "en": "because the production server doesn't care.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.73,
          "end": 61.95,
          "en": "So when you deploy your next project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.95,
          "end": 64.05,
          "en": "you therefore technically don't even have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.05,
          "end": 66.09,
          "en": "to deploy the public folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.09,
          "end": 68.763,
          "en": "NextJS is not interested in it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.41,
          "end": 73.65,
          "en": "Now, that's, of course, a problem for our app here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.65,
          "end": 78.65,
          "en": "because we do store images in that public folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.99,
          "end": 81.6,
          "en": "Well, this behavior is described",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.6,
          "end": 84.48,
          "en": "in the official NextJS documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.48,
          "end": 86.88,
          "en": "and there they therefore recommend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.88,
          "end": 91.02,
          "en": "that you should store any files that are generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.02,
          "end": 96.02000000000001,
          "en": "at run time, essentially, using extra file storage services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.09,
          "end": 98.253,
          "en": "like AWS S3.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.3,
          "end": 102.9,
          "en": "Now, since working with a provider like S3",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.9,
          "end": 105.24000000000001,
          "en": "is now really a bit beyond the scope",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.24000000000001,
          "end": 108.33,
          "en": "of this course, we'll ignore this problem here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.33,
          "end": 111.81,
          "en": "However, after this lecture, in the next lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.81,
          "end": 114.81,
          "en": "you'll find a text lecture where I do describe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.81,
          "end": 117.87,
          "en": "how you could use AWS S3",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 117.87,
          "end": 122.87,
          "en": "for storing and serving your user-generated images.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.88,
          "end": 125.04,
          "en": "You don't have to implement that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.04,
          "end": 126.9,
          "en": "You can ignore it for this demo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.9,
          "end": 130.11,
          "en": "but if you're interested in learning how that would work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130.11,
          "end": 132.033,
          "en": "that next lecture is for you.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}